%% For tabular environment
\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}
\usepackage{makecell}
\usetikzlibrary{calc} 
\usepackage{tkz-euclide}
\usetkzobj{all}
\usepackage{mathrsfs}

\begin{document}

\definecolor{deepskyblue}{rgb}{0.173,0.447,0.682}
\definecolor{orangepeel}{rgb}{0.902, 0.624, 0}
\definecolor{lightyellow}{rgb}{0.953,0.882,0.388}
\definecolor{darkgreen}{rgb}{0.271, 0.608, 0.463}
\definecolor{lightblue}{rgb}{0.484,0.702,0.894}
\definecolor{rustred}{rgb}{0.784,0.392,0.149}
\definecolor{fadedpink}{rgb}{0.753,0.494,0.643}
\definecolor{red}{rgb}{0.902, 0.624, 0}

\pagestyle{empty}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1.2]

\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (30:2.5);
\coordinate (C) at (90:2.5);
\coordinate (O) at (0:0);

% Angles
\tkzMarkAngle[fill=fadedpink, color=fadedpink, size=0.7cm](A,O,B);
\tkzLabelAngle[dist=1.4cm,yshift=-0.1cm](A,O,B){[math]8x+4^\circ[/math]};

\tkzMarkAngle[fill=lightblue, color=lightblue, size=0.7cm](B,O,C);
\tkzLabelAngle[dist=1cm](B,O,C){[math]46^\circ[/math]};

\tkzMarkRightAngle[size=.3,fill=orangepeel,opacity=0.8,color=orangepeel](A,O,C)

%Lines
\tkzDrawLines[add=0 and 1cm,very thick](O,A O,B O,C);

\end{tikzpicture}
\end{document}

Let's solve for [math]x[/math] given the figure above.

From the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so

\[
46^\circ + (8x + 4^\circ) = 90^\circ. 
\]

Hence, we can solve for [math]x[/math] as follows:

\begin{align*}
	46^\circ + (8x + 4^\circ) &= 90^\circ \\[3pt]
	8x + 50^\circ &= 90^\circ \\[3pt]
	8x &= 40^\circ \\[3pt]
	x &= 5^\circ
\end{align*}

